865	     * {@link #normalizeAddress(String)}). When a non-blank {@code addressLine1} is supplied the
866	     * structured form wins: {@code addressLine1} and {@code addressLine2} are stored normalized (an
867	     * absent or blank {@code addressLine2} is cleared) and the composed {@code address} is the
868	     * normalized {@code addressLine1}, with a single space and the normalized {@code addressLine2}
869	     * appended when the latter is present. When no {@code addressLine1} is supplied the flat
870	     * {@code address} is used unchanged for backward compatibility and the structured lines are
871	     * cleared. The composed {@code address} is what every later step reads.
